{
  "id": "u08-l06",
  "unit": "u08-daily-routine",
  "title": "How often?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Frequency words usually come early in the sentence, before the object and verb: **আমি প্রতিদিন অফিসে যাই** 'I go to the office every day'.\n\n- **প্রতিদিন** — every day\n- **সবসময়** — always\n- **মাঝে মাঝে** — sometimes\n- **কখনো … না** — never\n\nFor 'never', put **কখনো** before the verb and **না** after it: **আমি কখনো মাছ খাই না** 'I never eat fish'. As a one-word reply, **কখনো না!** 'Never!'\n\n**দাঁত মাজা** is 'brush (your) teeth': **আমি প্রতিদিন সকালে দাঁত মাজি** 'I brush my teeth every morning'. In cities many people use the English word 'brush' instead.\n\n**Culture:** Muslims say **নামাজ পড়া** — literally 'read the prayer'. **পড়েন** is the polite form, used for elders: **আমার দাদা সবসময় নামাজ পড়েন**. The call to prayer five times a day is one of the most familiar sounds of Bangladesh.",
  "vocab": [
